{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 — proven root cause)\n\n**Mechanism (confirmed).** `location /review/` uses the prefix-STRIPPING form\n`proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}/;` (rebar.conf.template:104), so the review-bot\nnever sees `/review/`. The app is a plain `uvicorn rebar.review_bot.app:app` FastAPI service —\n`FastAPI(title=…, summary=…, lifespan=…)` with **no `root_path`, no `redirect_slashes` override**\n(src/rebar/review_bot/app.py:491), routes `/health` `/webhook` `/rerun`, **no `RedirectResponse`\nanywhere** in `src/rebar/review_bot/`, and the Dockerfile CMD carries **no `--root-path`**\n(infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:171). Its only absolute redirects are Starlette's\n`redirect_slashes` 307s to its own routes, built from the forwarded `Host`. Post-a61d\n(`FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'`) that Location is `https://$host/<route>` — correct scheme, **no\n`/review/` prefix**. None of a61d's three rules match a `https://$host/...` Location (they match\n`http://…` prefixes and the loopback default), so the prefix is simply lost, the Location matches\nno review-bot route, falls through to `location /` → Gerrit → 404.\n\n**Runtime proof (real nginx 1.27-alpine + stub upstream emitting the Starlette-style absolute\nredirect).** Faithful copy of the current post-a61d `/review/` block vs. the same block plus the\nsingle new rule:\n\n    CURRENT:  GET /review/health/ (Host: example.test) -> 307 Location: https://example.test/health          <-- prefix LOST (repro)\n    FIXED:    GET /review/health/ (Host: example.test) -> 307 Location: https://example.test/review/health   <-- prefix RESTORED\n    BOTH:     GET /review/health  (Host: example.test) -> reaches app as /health                              <-- prefix-strip request path UNCHANGED\n    FIXED, a61d regression check (stub emits http://): -> 307 Location: https://example.test/health          <-- scheme still upgraded to https\n\n**Fix.** Add one rule to the `/review/` block, after a61d's scheme backstops (default stays first):\n`proxy_redirect https://$host/ https://$host/review/;`. nginx applies the first matching\n`proxy_redirect`; the new rule's `https://$host/` prefix overlaps none of the existing rules\n(which match `http://…`), so it neither shadows nor is shadowed by them — a61d's scheme guarantee\nand the prefix-stripping request path are both preserved. Confirmed on real nginx above.\n\n**Legitimacy = defect.** Violates the design contract that `/review/<route>/` must resolve to the\nreview-bot route, not a Gerrit 404 (ticket AC; a61d's sibling fix on the same block). Restoration,\nnot creation — no new capability, no new dependency.\n\n**Caller/dependency sweep.** The changed artifact is a response-header rewrite on one location\nblock; the only \"callers\" are HTTP clients following the `/review/` Location. No behavioral\ndependency on the prefix-less Location exists (it 404s today). Request-URI handling for the app is\nuntouched (proven above).\n\n**Defect attribution (caused_by).** `git blame -w -M -C` of rebar.conf.template:103-104 → commit\n`6cd6f4e1f7c0` (\"S2 (786b): deploy Gerrit + review-bot receiver behind nginx/TLS\"), a\nnew-file-creation commit (no carrier to walk through). That commit introduced the `/review/`\nlocation block AND its prefix-stripping `proxy_pass` together; the app's Starlette `redirect_slashes`\nabsolute-URL behaviour is default-framework behaviour present since the block's creation. The\nprefix loss was therefore **latent from day one — never a regression**. → caused_by\n**786b-190d-5e3a-4194** (smelly-pane-bolt), close-class **preexisting**. (Arguable as `plan_defect`\nsince 786b's edge-setup plan omitted the prefix-restore; `preexisting` is the precise match because\nthe behaviour was latent-from-creation, not broken by a later change.)\n\n**Residual (bounded).** The rule is a broad same-host rewrite: were the app ever to emit an\nabsolute redirect to a genuine non-`/review/` target on the same host, it would be wrongly\nprefixed. Bounded by a guard comment in the template + a test pinning the review-bot redirect\nsurface as same-app-only (no `RedirectResponse`, no `root_path`, no cross-host/off-`/review/`\nabsolute redirect), which turns RED if the app ever grows one.\n\n**Live-validation AC (edge probe) is DEFERRED to the operator edge-deploy** that also clears\na61d's AC5 (gated on bug 1d1b + operator apply). Not deploying; not blocking on it."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788111243321312629,"uuid":"e31a22aa-54b8-45c4-99f1-8534bfbf5bd6"}